| # The control the fix must not disturb: a `.SHELLFLAGS` that is plain words a
| # command line could carry stays the direct launch it always was. `-c` has no
| # shell syntax, so the tokenizer splits it, the launch execs `/bin/sh` `-c`
| # `<line>` directly, and the recipe runs — the same before the launch decision
| # learned to ask about the flags and after.
| #
| # THE GATE IS THE FILE `out`, written on the direct argv path a default SHELL
| # with plain flags takes.
| SHELL := /bin/sh
| .SHELLFLAGS := -c
| all:
| 	@echo one > out
file out touched 1
